    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Schrodinger&#x27;s third 1926 paper introduced his perturbation theory; here it is applied to a harmonic oscillator with an added quartic term. Checks quartic_perturbation_first_order_correction&#x27;s first-order Rayleigh-Schrodinger estimate against exact numerical diagonalization of the full anharmonic Hamiltonian (~chemistrykit.quantum.systems.perturbation.anharmonic_energy_levels, built in a truncated harmonic-oscillator basis via position_operator_matrix), and confirms that a cubic perturbation gives exactly zero first-order correction by parity.">

